# SAGE Phase Context

When working within a phase, the following context applies.

## Step sequence

Phases progress through 9 steps in strict order:

| Step | Code | What happens |
|------|------|--------------|
| S1 | dev-interview | Agent interviews developer; Plan mode only (no file writes) |
| S2 | implementation-plan | Agent produces implementation plan with TDD mapping |
| S3 | traceability-review | Agent checks PRD ↔ implementation plan bidirectionally |
| S4 | plan-validation | Agent produces plan preview; developer confirms |
| S5a | build (red) | test-author writes failing tests; produces red-results.md |
| S5b | build (green-refactor) | tdd-builder writes production code; produces tdd-results.md |
| S6 | code-review | Agent reviews code quality |
| S6.5 | security-review | Agent reviews code against SDLC policy and OWASP practices |
| S7 | agent-testing | Agent runs full test suite |
| S8 | completion-report | Agent produces completion report |

No step can begin until the prior step's required artifact exists.
This is enforced by the manifest-step-gate hook — not by instruction.

## Phase artifact naming convention

All artifacts use the pattern: `phase-{N}-{artifact-type}.md`

Where {N} is the phase number (e.g. phase-1, phase-2).

Examples:
- `phase-1-dev-interview-summary.md`
- `phase-1-implementation-plan.md`
- `phase-1-traceability-review.md`
- `phase-1-plan-preview.canvas.tsx`
- `phase-1-red-results.md`
- `phase-1-tdd-results.md`
- `phase-1-code-review.md`
- `phase-1-security-review.md`
- `phase-1-test-results.md`
- `phase-1-completion-report.md`

## Gate conditions

| Gate | Condition to pass |
|------|------------------|
| plan-mode-enforcer | currentStep ≠ 'dev-interview' OR write targets dev-interview-summary.md |
| manifest-step-gate | Prior artifact exists (plan-validation also requires Blocker findings: 0) |
| phase-approval-gate | linearIssueStatus = 'Approved' |
| required-references-gate | All requiredReferences have been read |
| validation-confirmed-gate | validationConfirmed = true (set by developer) |
| foundation-verified-gate | foundationVerified = true (Dependent phases only) |
| batch-confirmation-gate | batches[N].confirmed = true (Checkpoint mode only) |
| protected-manifest-fields-gate | No protected fields (validationConfirmed, batches[*].confirmed, foundationVerified) changed |
| red-results-gate | phase-{N}-red-results.md contains 'STATUS: RED CONFIRMED' (S5b only) |
| tdd-results-gate | phase-{N}-tdd-results.md contains 'STATUS: PASS' |
| code-review-gate | phase-{N}-code-review.md contains 'Critical findings: 0' |
| security-review-gate | phase-{N}-security-review.md contains 'Critical findings: 0' |
| completion-report-stop-gate | phase-{N}-test-results.md contains 'STATUS: PASS' |

## Domain source verification

Before referencing specific database objects, measures, data boundaries,
return codes, or flags, verify from the PRD, manifest `requiredReferences`,
and scoped code/schema. Do not assume domain details from prior knowledge.

As of the current specification — verify before generating scenarios,
proofs, or reviews:
- Output measures may be defined in views such as `vw_BI_AllInstruments`
  and `Global_Result` — confirm the exact view and measure set from the PRD
  and scoped schema
- Data boundary (e.g. Dataverse for GL and reference data) — confirm from
  the PRD and architecture documentation
- Return codes (e.g. -1 through -8) — confirm which codes apply from the
  TDD spec and scoped stored procedures
- Flags (e.g. `NewInstFlag`, `ClosedInstFlag`, `PlugInstrumentFlag`) —
  confirm applicability from the scoped code
- Naming inconsistencies exist in the codebase — always verify against
  the actual schema before writing specs or reviews
